// open-list — COMPILES CLEAN AND IS SILENTLY WRONG, which is the row no filing
// had caught. `Shape([int])` reads as "a one-element list of int"; `int` is
// lowercase in pattern position, so it is a BINDER NAMED int. For `list<int>`
// the declared parameter type already constrains the element, so the pasted
// clause behaves correctly — which is precisely why nothing noticed. Change the
// element type and the same spelling is wrong.
module OpenList

public atom Shape(list<int> xs)
Shape([]) -> :empty
Shape([a, b, ..]) -> :many
